The Clinic System Activity Diagram is shown below.The following is the detailed explanation of the Clinic System Activity Diagram.
Introduction
This UML Activity Diagram depicts the activity sequence of Clinic Management System. The system enables a patient to:
register/login,book an appointment,Pay consultation fee,attend consultation,order medication,and full payment of medications.
The diagram represents the interaction of various elements of the system from start to finish.Swimlanes in the Diagram
The diagram has three swimlanes.
1. Patient Swimlane
All Activities of the Patient are located in this section.
Examples:
Login/Register
Book Appointment
Make Payment
Order Medication
2. Clinic System Swimlane
These are system processes included in this section.
Examples:
Check Doctor Availability
Generate Invoice
Confirm Appointment
Confirm Medication Order
3. Payment Gateway Swimlane
This is the process that deals with online payment transactions.
Examples:
Process Booking Fee Payment.
Process Medication Payment
Brief notes and explanations for each step.

1. Start
It starts at the black filled circle (first node).
This represents the beginning of the clinic's workflow.

2. Login / Register
The first step in the process of the patient entering the system is:
Signing up for a new account,When an existing account is being used, login in.This step provides for safe access to clinic services.

3. Book Appointment
Once the patient logs on, he/she requests an appointment with the clinic.
This is an information to the clinic system for processing.

4. Receive Appointment Request
The clinic system accepts the appointment booking request from the patient.
System is preparing to check doctor availability.

5. Check Doctor Availability
The clinic system checks:available doctors,available dates,and time slots.
This way, the doctor that you choose is available during the time that you want.

6. Decision: Slot Available?
A diamond with two arrows leading outwards is a decision node.
There are two alternatives:
If NO
The selected slot is out of stock,The patient will have to choose another doctor, date, and time.The flow then recirculates back to:Select Doctor, Date & Time”
If YES
The appointment process is ongoing.The system then starts to create the invoice.

7. Click on Doctor & Date & Time.
The patient chooses:doctor name,appointment date,appointment time.
This information is necessary in order to confirm your booking.

8. Generate a Contracts Report.10. Generate an Invoice (Booking Fee).
The clinic system gives out:booking fee,consultation charge.

Then the system prints out the payment invoice.

9.Process Payment (Booking Fee)
The payment details are then passed on to the Payment Gateway.
The gateway securely processes the online payment.

10. Decision: Payment Successful?
Next, there is another decision node for payment status.
If NO
payment failed,patient retries payment.
If YES
payment is accepted,appointment is confirmed.

11. Confirm Appointment
The appointment is confirmed by the clinic system.
Confirmation information is given to the patient.

12. Conduct Consultation
Patient visits the clinic and consults with the physician.
The doctor examines the patient.

13. Decision: Medication Required?
The doctor after consultation concludes whether or not a medication is required.
If NO
no medicine required,process ends.
If YES
Patient continues to medication order process.

14. Order Medication
The patient calls the hospital to get the medicines that they are ordered to take.
Order is recorded in the clinic system.

15. Confirm Medication Order
The clinic system verifies:
medicine availability,order details.The order is then confirmed.

16. Process Payment (Medication)
Medication fee is paid by the patient.
The payment gateway executes the payment.

17. Decision: Payment Successful?
If NO


patient retries payment.
If YES
medication payment succeeds.Clinic is conducted with delivery/pickup.

18. Provide Order to Patient
The clinic system offers medicine to the patient via:
clinic pickup,or delivery service.

19. Receive Medication
Patient is able to take the medication.

20. End
The process stops at the last node (black circle with outer boundary).
This shows that they have passed:appointment booking,consultation,and medication process.

Overall System Workflow:
The clinic activity diagram illustrates the overall patient's journey:
Patient logs in to system.
Patient books appointment.
Checks doctor availability for the system.
Booking fee is paid and generated.
Appointment gets confirmed.
Patient attends consultation.
Medication is determined by Doctor.
Patient self orders medication if necessary.
Medication payment is made.
Patient receives medicine.
Process ends successfully.

Conclusion
This activity diagram helps visualize how the clinic system operates step-by-step. It clearly shows:
patient interactions,internal clinic processing,and payment handling.The swimlane design helps to clarify the issues by dividing duties between:Patient,Clinic System,and Payment Gateway.This will simplify the system analysis, development and management.